==English==
===Etymology===
Compound of [[red]] + [[neck]] (referring to the sunburn on the neck typical of rural farm workers).

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

#{{context|slang}} An uneducated, unsophisticated, or poor white person, typically used to describe residents of the [[rural]] Southern US.
#{{context|slang}} The nickname given to miners who wore red bandanas for identification during the West Virginia mine war of 1921.  http://www.wvculture.org/hiStory/minewars.html


